Z||000000||VAROOM||11-13-1999||04:40 PM||||Does any one know where to get a picture or diagram of the vacume lines for the cruse control on my 87 GT ??? is there any place on lin to down load this info. Thanks were still tryingto get this thing to run...!     ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||11-13-1999||09:55 PM||||Likely not..... there is only one vac line for the cruise. The cruise and it's vac reserve can will work off any source of manifold vacuum.<P>vacuum line goes from manifold vac to the reserve can output side, then from the vac reserve in side to the cruise.<P>The manifild vac source can be either the large vapor canister purge line or a port anywhere on the intake manifold.<P>The other "port" on the cruise unit is it's vent. Which should have a filter on it but often it doesn't.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||11-15-1999||07:21 AM||||I bought the JC Whitney OEM Look VSS cruise control unit but haven't installed it yet.  I'm still in the middle of an engine transplant.<BR>Anyway, the instructions caution against tieing into the large vacuum line that supplies vacuum to the power brakes.<P>Since my 85SE 2m6  4spd did not originally come with cruise I am also looking for a convenient vacuum port to tie into.  I noticed a tee in one of the steel vacuum lines that serves the fuel vapor canister right close to where the vacuum canister will mount.  I'll give that a try first.||||reg||1
